{
    "background_story": "Benicio was a rugged, old-world farmer who lived in the rolling hills of rural Spain. He spent his days tending to his land, using traditional methods passed down from his ancestors. One of his most prized possessions was an antique whiffletree, a wooden beam used to balance the weight of a plow or wagon. Benicio's whiffletree had been in his family for generations, its worn surface telling the story of countless harvests and hard-won battles against the elements. He took great care to preserve the whiffletree, using it to teach his children and grandchildren the value of hard work and tradition. As the years went by, Benicio's farm became a symbol of the region's rich heritage, with the whiffletree standing as a testament to the enduring power of simplicity and dedication.",
